      "message": "Agreed it isn\u0027t valid...however, it\u0027s used equivalently in the codebase as the proper 4.\n```\nenum AddressType : 8 {\n  PUBLIC_DEVICE_ADDRESS \u003d 0x00,\n  RANDOM_DEVICE_ADDRESS \u003d 0x01,\n  PUBLIC_IDENTITY_ADDRESS \u003d 0x02,\n  RANDOM_IDENTITY_ADDRESS \u003d 0x03,\n}\n```\n\nI think this retrieved from the LE EXTENDED ADVERTISING REPORT which is the only type I can find that uses the `anonymous` term\n\n```\nValue Parameter Description\n0x00 Public Device Address\n0x01 Random Device Address\n0x02 Public Identity Address (corresponds to Resolved Private Address)\n0x03 Random (static) Identity Address (corresponds to Resolved Private\nAddress)\n0xFF No address provided (anonymous advertisement)\nAll other values Reserved for future use\n```\n\nWould you like me to remove the `BLE_ADDR_ANONYMOUS` case statement ? \n(It will be caught by default anyway)",
