      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree it\u0027s confusing, and I can\u0027t answer your contextual questions.\n\nThe idea here is to provide the same functionality embedded in the legacy code but in a much more sane manner.\n\nIt\u0027s still used in system/stack/btm/btm_ble_addr.cc and system/stack/btm/btm_ble_gap.cc , but it\u0027s unclear if it actually does anything.\n\nThe idea is to reclaim the ability to arbitrarily manipulate and check this in non-relevant portions of the stack.\n\nMy hope/guess is that these are band-aids to simplify the legacy stack, and once the legacy is straightened out, these will disappear when no longer used. \n\nI wish functions had reference count, and auto-deleted them selves when nobody calls.",
